 ("Fedora installed on the tablet", "ok", "22 Oct 2026: the installed system is Fedora 44 with GNOME 50 on kernel q90i (7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00463, the only boot entry), iceland-device 0.28-32, iceland-coexist 1.0-6, upower 1.91.5-1.fc44.iceland1, iceland-firmware 11.A.38-6 and U-Boot v7 in boot_b; the root is on device-mapper with TRIM, USB-C runtime PM is on. Before: 19 Oct 2026: the installed system runs kernel q89w (7.3.0-rc7-iceland-00519, the default; the Wi-Fi PCIe link at Gen3 through a device-tree override on the default entry), iceland-device 0.28-29, iceland-firmware 11.A.38-6 and U-Boot v7 in boot_b (the dual boot BlissROM + Fedora since 17 Oct). Before: 16 Oct 2026 evening: the installed system runs kernel q89m (7.3.0-rc7-iceland-00453), iceland-device 0.28-20, iceland-firmware 11.A.38-6 (the vendor GPU firmware v5.3.33 with GPU preemption on) and U-Boot v4 in boot_b; every update since 14 Oct came through dnf from an owner-installed update bundle. Before: Installed 13 Oct 2026 (evening) with the owner's two writes, after the checks G1 (151 backup files intact), G2, G3 (stock restore dry run) and G4 (a second backup copy): write 1 = userdata <- the B149 install image (sha256 2246e9a7; 9 of 9 sparse pieces OKAY, 267 s), write 2 = boot_b <- the footered U-Boot install build v3 (4955ee98). Only userdata and boot_b were written. Since write 2 Fedora boots on its own from boot_b (ABL -> U-Boot -> GRUB -> kernel; the root is btrfs on a loop device in userdata). The install is closed: an ABL read on 14 Oct shows slot b successful yes and its retry count staying at 3 (the owner's hand mark holds; see Boot slot marked good from Fedora). Since 14 Oct the tablet runs kernel q89h (dnf, trial boot, confirmed default; see Kernel package), 0.28-10's power-key guard and 0.28-8's thermal file (both by hand) and the field report's local tuning (see Device package). The first night unplugged used about 0.22 W (see Deep-sleep proof). 16 Oct 2026 late: kernel q89m (00453) is the confirmed GRUB default (the 0.28-20 --check: trial / kernel confirmed 00453). Open owner findings being fixed: mid-session 0.8 s vblank-timeout stalls (since q89k), an iio-sensor-proxy hang at suspend (2 of 14), the RTC offset missing on one boot.", "Owner check: the listening check (+9 dB), the physical checks (cover wake, USB host, DP monitor, keyboard cover, a USB-C PD charger)"),
 ("Boot slot marked good from Fedora", "ok", "22 Oct 2026: confirmed working by the owner on 22 Oct 2026. Before: 16 Oct 2026 evening: the remaining failure is fixed in iceland-device 0.28-17: the 16 Oct issue scan (q89k) found iceland-slot-mark failing every boot (a oneshot unit inside the boot transaction waited for itself, the system stayed in starting for 300 s); now Type=exec with RuntimeMaxSec (package tests 52 / 52). The fix is in every later package and on the tablet with 0.28-18 to 0.28-20; the confirming scan on the installed system is pending. Before: iceland-slot-mark (iceland-device 0.27r5 on) runs qbootctl -m once after a good boot and is guarded off in RAM kits and rehearsals (I1 PASS in r139b / r139c). On the installed system (13-14 Oct) it skipped every boot ('/ is on /dev/loop0p3': the installed root is a loop device on userdata), and boot_b's LUN is read-only under iceland-storage-ro; ABL's retry count for slot b fell 7 -> 3. The owner marked slot b by hand (14 Oct ~00:0x; the LUN writable for that one command, then read-only again). The ABL read of 14 Oct: slot b successful yes, retry count staying at 3 = the mark holds. The package fix (0.28-8, 61dbe569; the loop0 detail corrected in 0.28-9) accepts a loop root backed by userdata, matches the partition by its label (the LUN names vary per boot: sda15 / sdb15) and makes the boot LUN writable only for the one qbootctl -m: test_slot_mark PASS, PC tests only, not yet in an image, a rehearsal or on the tablet.", "Nothing"),
 ("Dual boot BlissROM + Fedora", "ok", "17 Oct 2026: the power-on menu of U-Boot v7 (boot_b) offers Fedora / BlissROM / Boot loader, and both systems start from it on the tablet. LUN 0 is split in place: fedora 124.86 GiB (Fedora's bytes unmoved; its btrfs shrunk to 120 GiB and its own table shrunk first), userdata 96.01 GiB for BlissROM v20.1 (f2fs, encrypted; erased together with metadata before the first start), and the last 1 MiB of LUN 0 left unpartitioned (ABL writes near the LUN end at slot-flag updates). The OnePlus ABL starts recovery_b only without a kernel (then with boot_b's kernel, U-Boot), so the BlissROM entry runs qcom_android_chain (iceland-u-boot 0015): the kernel of BlissROM's boot.img from boot_a, booted with the vendor_boot_b + init_boot_b ramdisks, bootconfig and DT that ABL prepared for boot_b. BlissROM's slot-b boot parts and its system (one super image built with tools/dualboot mk-super.py and checked with check-super.py) are flashed by ABL; Fedora boots from the fedora partition. Guide: docs/DUAL-BOOT.md.", "Add: a BlissROM update procedure (new boot_a, slot-b boot parts and super image); Add: a U-Boot v7 release"),
 ("Virtual machines (Gunyah)", "ok", "27 Oct 2026: published as iceland-gvm 0.3-59 (crosvm: 30 patches on 96e84c3f680e, release/0.3-59 = 0.3-58's 29 + the virtio keyboard declaring Super) and iceland-vms 0.2-23 (the app at release/0.2-16 0dfd09b) with the new package iceland-vms-guest-mesa 26.2.5-1.iceland1 (packaging in iceland-vms packaging/nctx-mesa); every file in the RPMs scanned clean. On q90w2: Super through the shortcuts option and the msm native context pass, regression (virgl, shared + venus, QEMU) PASS, no host kernel warnings (rows below). 26 Oct 2026 (night): published as iceland-gvm 0.3-58 (crosvm: 29 patches on 96e84c3f680e, release branch release/0.3-58 = 0.3-55's 28 + the keyboard grab), virglrenderer 1.3.0-1.iceland1 (Fedora 44's 1.3.0 + four upstream Venus fixes; RPMs in the 0.3-58 release, sources in iceland-gvm virglrenderer/) and iceland-vms 0.2-22 (the app at release/0.2-16 2d7a762); every file in the RPMs scanned clean. On q90w2: the app's clean Windows Shut Down, Vulkan and zink in the shared-memory mode, the keyboard shortcuts option and the QEMU regression pass (rows below). 26 Oct 2026 (latest): published as iceland-vms 0.2-20 + the new package iceland-qemu-gunyah 10.0.2-1 (GitHub release 0.2-20 of iceland-vms; QEMU sources: 11 patches on QEMU v10.0.2 in iceland-vms qemu-gunyah/; the app at release/0.2-16 347216e; every file in both rpms scanned clean; iceland-gvm 0.3-55 unchanged): the QEMU-Gunyah backend with 3D OpenGL and 3D OpenGL in the shared-memory mode (rows below). 26 Oct 2026 (later): published as iceland-gvm 0.3-55 + iceland-vms 0.2-18 (GitHub releases; 28 crosvm patches on 96e84c3f680e, the app at cdef65e; every file in both rpms scanned clean): the opt-in shared-memory mode (next rows). Release run on q90u: 58 PASS; the two FAILs are excluded features (WA-7 the app's clean Windows Shut Down, PV-B-3 3D in the shared mode). 26 Oct 2026: published as iceland-gvm 0.3-49 + iceland-vms 0.2-17 (GitHub releases; sources: 26 crosvm patches on 96e84c3f680e, the app at release/0.2-16 3e746e4; firmware and gunyah_guest.ko built from neutral /build paths; every file in both rpms scanned clean). Release run on q90u: V1B 4/4, WINAPP WA-1..6 PASS (import, running, arguments, address, RDP, ssh), WA-7 (the app's clean Windows Shut Down) FAIL - excluded, Windows is shut down from inside Windows or with Force Off; K-ALL PASS. 26 Oct 2026: the VM stack's next release (iceland-gvm 0.3-4x / iceland-vms 0.2-1x, not published yet) adds the Windows 11 ARM guest through gvm.sh, touch input modes, a VNC display, 2 MiB memory lends and io_uring disks (rows below); the VM release run on kernel q90u: V1B, the 3D desktop, the software display, VNC, touch and userspace networking PASS. 25 Oct 2026: protected VMs work with crosvm on Gunyah: iceland-gvm 0.3-27 (crosvm 96e84c3f680e + 12 patches, a guest kernel with DroidVM's gunyah_guest built in and the virtio-gpu EXECBUFFER sync through the restricted DMA pool) and the Virtual Machines app iceland-vms 0.2-5 on kernel q90r (the Gunyah VM manager is in the kernel since q90m). Fedora 44 Cloud guests on virtio disks with NAT (DHCP, DNS, HTTPS, dnf), serial console, ssh and a clean power-off through the guest agent; 3D with virgl (OpenGL) and venus (Vulkan): Xorg glamor, weston GL, the Xfce desktop and the labwc Wayland session draw in the VM window, which is opaque (vm-run v10e and v10i, K-ALL PASS, no host kernel warnings); the shared-framebuffer software display (V8 PASS) and 2D as fallbacks; guest glmark2 offscreen 9.0-9.3k through virgl on the Adreno 840 (llvmpipe 120-160). The owner accepted VM 3D as working on 25 Oct 2026. Sources: github.com/mzakamin-hub/iceland-gvm and iceland-vms. Before: 17 Oct 2026: protected VMs run a Linux guest. On kernel 7.3.0-rc7-iceland-00456 the Gunyah VM-manager modules load (hypervisor 51/v1, /dev/gunyah); a protected VM with 4 MiB lent memory and 1 vCPU starts, takes MMIO exits, writes a hello text and powers off with an EXITED status in 5 of 5 runs; a Linux 7.3 guest kernel boots in a protected VM with 64 MiB lent memory (GICv3, arch timer, PSCI, serial console over MMIO exits) to its /init and powers off cleanly; all 10 modules unload afterwards. Side package packaging/gunyah (SuperTurtleDev's import of Android's Gunyah drivers + our fixes), not in the kernel queue; protected VMs only (the firmware refuses unprotected VMs).", "Add: ISO installs through edk2-gunyah"),
 ("Windows 11 ARM guest VM (gvm tool)", "ok", "26 Oct 2026 (night): Shut Down from the app works (iceland-vms 0.2-22): the app offers its own key and the user's default ssh key, installs its own key in the guest once (administrators_authorized_keys), then runs shutdown /s over ssh; the VM was off in 7 s with a clean exit. When Windows refuses ssh the app says so at once and offers Force Off. 26 Oct 2026: also inside the Virtual Machines app (iceland-vms 0.2-17): import a prepared image, start, the Remote Desktop button, ssh (WA-1..6 PASS on q90u); shut down from inside Windows or with Force Off. 25-26 Oct 2026: Windows 11 ARM64 runs as a protected Gunyah VM started with gvm.sh win (ECAM UEFI firmware, simplefb screen, NAT, DroidVM's test-signed Windows drivers): full session on 25 Oct with iceland-gvm 0.3-35: network and DHCP, the RDP port, ssh, desktop drawn, HTTPS, x86 emulation, 10 min load, a 30 min soak and a restart, clean shutdown, no host freeze in about 90 min (K-ALL PASS); only the driver-list row failed. 26 Oct: a fresh Setup on q90u reached the desktop and RDP (W2 / W3-1 / W3-R / W4-1 PASS; ssh not installed in time).", "Nothing"),
 ("VM window touch input modes", "ok", "26 Oct 2026: published in iceland-gvm 0.3-49 / iceland-vms 0.2-17. 25-26 Oct 2026: the crosvm window maps touch in three modes - tablet (tap = click, drag, long press and two-finger tap = right click, two-finger scroll), touchpad (relative pointer) and touch screen (multi-finger) - with fullscreen on a chosen monitor; logical-to-pixel scaling at scale 2 and both screen rotations: rows VINX and VINROT all PASS (p5, uinput touch injector, guest evdev recorder); VINX PASS again in the VM release run.", "Nothing"),
 ("VM VNC display", "ok", "26 Oct 2026: published in iceland-gvm 0.3-49 / iceland-vms 0.2-17 (a viewer button on the VM's page; local only, or on the network with a password). 26 Oct 2026: crosvm's VNC server (port of DroidVM's, LibVNCServer) exports a running VM's screen; row V9 VNC PASS in the VM release run (iceland-gvm 0.3-43 / iceland-vms 0.2-13) on kernel q90u.", "Nothing"),
 ("VM memory and disk speed (2 MiB lends, io_uring)", "ok", "26 Oct 2026: published in iceland-gvm 0.3-49 / iceland-vms 0.2-17 (2 MiB pages, io_uring for every disk, the shared I/O bounce buffer capped at 320 MiB). 25 Oct 2026 (kit v10m OPT): guest memory lent in 2 MiB blocks: VM boot 52.5 -> 10.6 s, touching 1 GiB 25.6 -> 9.2 s, TrustZone calls 1.03 M -> 174 k; the io_uring disk engine: 3.3 GB/s read, 1.3 GB/s write in the guest (the fastest variant; O_DIRECT and more workers gave nothing). io_uring is the default disk engine of the app and gvm.sh from iceland-gvm 0.3-42; the Windows app VM uses 2 MiB lends.", "Tune: THP fallbacks to 4 KiB donations after fragmentation"),
 ("VM fast networking (vhost-net)", "ok", "26 Oct 2026: the in-kernel virtio-net path (vhost-net, CONFIG_VHOST_NET=m since q90s) is on by default in iceland-gvm 0.3-49 / iceland-vms 0.2-17 and can be switched off per VM; TCP over the NAT tap, 15 s each way, guest -> host / host -> guest: crosvm's own network 2420 / 1959 MB/s, vhost-net 2877 / 4761 MB/s (V11 PASS). Kernels older than q90s fall back to crosvm's own network.", "Nothing"),
 ("VM shared-memory mode (partial protection)", "ok", "26 Oct 2026 (night): Vulkan (venus) and OpenGL through zink also work in this mode, on by default (iceland-vms 0.2-22, feature memory_shared_vulkan; virglrenderer 1.3.0-1.iceland1): Venus device on the Adreno 840, host-visible blob memory, glmark2 about 1820 at 1280x800, zink over Venus. The native GPU context is still refused in this mode. 26 Oct 2026 (later): 3D OpenGL (virgl) works in this mode (iceland-vms 0.2-20, feature memory_shared_3d): the earlier PV-B-3 failure was the test (glmark2 without access to the render node); on q90v the app's shared + virgl VM drew with renderer virgl on the Adreno 840, glmark2 1799 at 1280x800 (gvm's corrected PV-B-3 on q90u: 1634). Vulkan (venus / zink) and the native context have not run in this mode and stay refused. 26 Oct 2026: opt-in per VM in iceland-vms 0.2-18 (Settings > Memory > Memory protection > Shared with the tablet; software display or headless): the VM still runs under Gunyah but its RAM is shared with the tablet instead of lent - DroidVM's boot shim accepts the memory and starts the kernel, so there is no I/O bounce buffer and devices reach guest memory directly. Warning shown whenever selected: the tablet can read and change all of that VM's memory; Protected stays the default. Measured against the same VM protected (shared / protected): disk write 256 MiB fsync 260 / 397 MB/s (-35 %), cold disk read 450 / 430 MB/s (about the same), network guest -> host 4494 / 2611 MB/s (+72 %), host -> guest 1484 / 1940 MB/s (-23 %). Release run PV rows PASS except PV-B-3 (3D in this mode: not supported yet).", "Nothing"),
 ("VM QEMU-Gunyah backend (3D OpenGL)", "ok", "26 Oct 2026: iceland-vms 0.2-20 + iceland-qemu-gunyah 10.0.2-1 (QEMU v10.0.2 + the Gunyah accelerator of qemu-gunyah/qemu-android-gunyah 1eee442b + 10 fixes: fixed 256 MB lend chunks, shared regions populated before the share, the kernel ioeventfd, virgl fences through virglrenderer's sync thread by default; edk2-gunyah-qemu 50c9eb78 firmware): Settings > General > Backend, crosvm stays the default. Protected VMs under QEMU (guest RAM in a memfd, lent) with 3D OpenGL (virgl, virtio-gpu-gl) on the Adreno 840 in QEMU's GTK window or over VNC (egl-headless). On q90v through the app: clone, start, ssh, renderer virgl (Adreno 840), glmark2 1280x800 about 1390-1410 in the window and over VNC (crosvm 1764), a clean Shut Down (QEMU exit 0), no host kernel warnings. Vulkan (venus / zink) and the native context stay crosvm-only (refused on QEMU with the reason).", "Nothing"),
 ("VM keyboard shortcuts (Send shortcuts to the VM)", "ok", "27 Oct 2026: Super reaches the guest too (iceland-gvm 0.3-59: the virtio keyboard declares the Super keys; the guest's input core dropped undeclared keys): Super, Alt+Tab and Escape all arrive. 26 Oct 2026: iceland-vms 0.2-22 + iceland-gvm 0.3-58 (Settings > Display > Send shortcuts to the VM, off by default): the crosvm window asks the compositor to pass its shortcuts to the VM while it has the keyboard focus (keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit-unstable-v1). On q90w2 under KDE Plasma: Alt+Tab and Escape reach the guest; the Super key is still kept by the desktop.", "Nothing"),
 ("VM native GPU context (msm)", "ok", "27 Oct 2026: iceland-vms 0.2-23 + iceland-gvm 0.3-59 + iceland-vms-guest-mesa 26.2.5-1.iceland1 (display 3D: msm native context, opt-in, off by default): the app delivers a guest Mesa 26.2.5 built with freedreno's virtio kernel-mode driver (Fedora's builds msm only, so it fell back to llvmpipe) and the guest agent sets it up. On q90w2: GL renderer Adreno (TM) 840 through the msm native context, glmark2 2691 at 1280x800 (virgl 1768), turnip Vulkan on the Adreno 840 in the guest, no crosvm errors, no host kernel warnings.", "Nothing"),
